    "relevance": 7,
    "significance": "This work directly tackles the practical implantation challenge for speech BCIs: where and how densely to place electrodes on the sensorimotor cortex to decode spoken words reliably while managing surgical and safety trade-offs. By characterizing the relationship between grid size, positioning, and classification accuracy, the study provides design specifications for the next generation of clinical speech BCIs. This is core neurotechnology development work that bridges neuroscience findings to hardware deployment decisions."
